{"kind":"charness.bounded_review.v1","lens":"release-critique","packet_sha256":"b0abe4204666fc2a8133c6099bf76197634de5c31667247f13563f324d64b692","reviewed_input_identity_sha256":"da187164719b3b95fc1eecc2f6bda5cc69faf7494e7e1cc7d6e7ec89399ddd5d","verdict":"block","target_observations":null,"findings":[{"id":"REL-820-1","severity":"blocker","summary":"The real Node acceptance tests omit the TAP reporter flag required by the implementation.","evidence":["tests/quality_gates/test_mutation_test_reporters.py invokes node with [\"node\", \"--test\"] in every end-to-end #820 case.","NodeTestReporter intentionally refuses spec output and requires --test-reporter=tap; unreadable_refusal() explicitly names that escape hatch.","Therefore the acceptance path can refuse a green baseline instead of proving kill/refuse/survive behavior, depending on Node's default reporter."],"action":"Make every Node/TAP verification command explicitly include --test-reporter=tap, and assert the release-time command surface uses the same setting."},{"id":"REL-820-2","severity":"blocker","summary":"Manifest synchronization and packaging verification are identified but not demonstrated as release gates.","evidence":["The packet lists sync_root_plugin_manifests.py and packaging validators as owning-surface commands, but none of the reviewed code or tests invokes them.","No generated manifest, committed-export check, or pre-tag verification evidence is included.","A source-only commit can therefore be tagged while the materialized plugin export remains stale."],"action":"Run manifest sync before tagging, inspect and commit the resulting generated changes, then run both packaging validators from a fresh checkout and record their results."},{"id":"REL-820-3","severity":"high","summary":"Recovery and fresh-checkout operator closure are available as commands but are not part of the demonstrated release contract.","evidence":["--check-recovery and --recover provide operator signals, while run_sweep() only calls assert_clear() at sweep start.","The reviewed tests do not exercise SIGKILL/untrappable interruption, pending-journal detection, recovery, or a fresh-checkout doctor sequence.","The packet supplies no evidence that a release operator will detect and clear an interrupted mutation before verification or tagging."],"action":"Add an Act-Before-Ship checklist/gate: run doctor or --check-recovery, simulate or consume an interrupted journal, verify --recover and byte restoration, and repeat the relevant Node/TAP and packaging checks from a clean checkout."}],"counterweight_triage":[{"concern":"The kill/refuse/survive contract may be implemented at the wrong layer.","bin":"not a blocker","disposition":"The split is appropriate: the reporter owns runner-specific counts and named failures; classification owns verdicts. Named-test mismatch refuses, green runs survive, and matching failures kill."},{"concern":"Call-site reachability is not mechanically established for Node/JavaScript targets.","bin":"real limitation","disposition":"The Python AST check is explicitly inapplicable to .js and emits a non-claim. This is honest, but release notes and operator checks must not present #820 as proving production caller reachability."},{"concern":"Restore/journal lifecycle may silently leave mutations behind.","bin":"insufficient evidence","disposition":"The finally-based restore and byte verification are plausibly layered correctly, but the packet lacks interruption/recovery execution evidence; retain as an open verification item."}],"next_move":"Block the 8.9.0 tag until the Node commands explicitly select TAP, manifests are synchronized and packaging-validated, and recovery plus fresh-checkout operator checks produce recorded evidence.","non_claims":["This is a bounded packet review only; it does not establish that the tests pass in the current workspace.","No approval is inferred from the implementation's extensive self-tests or from the claimed end-to-end coverage.","The review was not Goal Run-bound, consistent with the supplied goal lineage."]}
